Theorem L-3: Lattice join idempotence

  Preconditions:
    - a is an AimsState element per the canonical proof notation
      sec-Per-Dimension-Symbol-Set
    - join is the product-lattice componentwise join per Annex E §AIMS + sec-1.8 L-3

  Soundness property:
    Forall a in AimsState. join(a, a) = a

  Proof obligation:
    Componentwise per-dimension finite enumeration over the 7 carriers
    proves dim_join_d(x, x) = x for every x. Product idempotence
    follows by componentwise lift.

    Per-dimension element counts (|carrier|):
      Access 2
      Consumption 4
      Cardinality 3
      Uniqueness 3
      Locality 5
      Shape 5
      Effect 8

    Total per-dimension enumeration: 30 singleton checks (one per
    element across the 7 carriers).

    Per-dimension argument:
      Access / Consumption / Cardinality / Uniqueness / Locality:
        max(x, x) = x on a totally ordered carrier — the predicate
        x >= x is reflexive, so max selects either argument and both
        are x.
      Shape (flat lattice):
        case_analysis(x == x -> x; x != x -> Phi); the first arm
        always fires because equality is reflexive.
      Effect (componentwise OR):
        OR(b, b) = b on Bool; per-flag idempotence composes
        componentwise.

    Lift to product:
      join(a, a) = (dim_join_d(a_d, a_d))_d
                 = (a_d)_d (per-dim L-3)
                 = a

    Sentinel handling: SCALAR pre-filtered per L-9; FRESH /
    CONSERVATIVE / ALL / NONE are concrete 7-tuples obeying
    componentwise idempotence.

    Engines dispatched:
      lattice (per-dimension finite enumeration discharge per
        section_02::verify_l3_idempotence)
      monotonicity (validates idempotence preserves L-6 monotonicity:
        idempotent joins on monotone lattices remain monotone)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: sec-02 lattice engine discharges L-3 via per-dimension finite enumeration over the 7 dimension carriers
